1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,686
When you write a theme in Razor, its views reach Orchard Core in two ways.

2
00:00:05,686 --> 00:00:10,664
The Orchard helper adds methods that load content, build URLs and convert text,

3
00:00:10,664 --> 00:00:13,593
and tag helpers render shapes and resources.

4
00:00:13,593 --> 00:00:16,170
This video shows what each one offers.

5
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:24,973
In a Razor view, Orchard is a property of the view's base class.

6
00:00:24,973 --> 00:00:29,417
A theme sets that base class once, with an inherits directive in its

7
00:00:29,417 --> 00:00:33,680
view imports file, and every view of the theme gets the property.

8
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:38,494
A view that doesn't use that base class, such as a Razor Page,

9
00:00:38,494 --> 00:00:41,721
injects I Orchard Helper under the name Orchard.

10
00:00:41,721 --> 00:00:45,785
A controller or a service takes it as a constructor parameter.

11
00:00:45,785 --> 00:00:49,430
The interface has one member, the current HTTP context.

12
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:56,432
The helpers are extension methods, and each module defines those of its own features:

13
00:00:56,432 --> 00:01:02,959
Contents, Alias, Autoroute, Media, Markdown, Queries, Lists and Taxonomies, among others.

14
00:01:02,959 --> 00:01:08,730
In a theme, add a reference to the module or package whose method isn't found.

15
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:14,155
Many helpers also call services that their module registers, so the module's feature

16
00:01:14,155 --> 00:01:16,232
has to be enabled on the site too.

17
00:01:16,232 --> 00:01:20,180
The reference makes the method compile, and the feature makes it work.

18
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:28,914
Four helpers load one content item from what you know of it:

19
00:01:28,914 --> 00:01:31,388
its id, alias, slug or handle.

20
00:01:31,388 --> 00:01:37,227
A handle combines a prefix, such as alias, slug or contentitemid, with a value.

21
00:01:37,227 --> 00:01:40,800
Each helper returns null when nothing matches.

22
00:01:41,550 --> 00:01:44,864
These helpers return the published version by default.

23
00:01:44,864 --> 00:01:49,337
The alias and slug helpers take a Boolean flag for the most recent version.

24
00:01:49,337 --> 00:01:53,479
The handle and id helpers take Version Options, which can ask for the

25
00:01:53,479 --> 00:01:56,020
most recent version, draft or published.

26
00:01:56,770 --> 00:02:01,921
To list items, Get Recent Content Items By Content Type Async returns the

27
00:02:01,921 --> 00:02:05,964
published items of a type, newest first, ten by default.

28
00:02:05,964 --> 00:02:12,420
For any other condition, Query Content Items Async takes a query over the content item index.

29
00:02:13,170 --> 00:02:17,283
To render an item, call Display Async with the item and a display

30
00:02:17,283 --> 00:02:18,905
type, such as Summary.

31
00:02:18,905 --> 00:02:22,381
It returns rendered markup, which the view writes out.

32
00:02:22,381 --> 00:02:27,362
Where Model is dynamic, the view casts the item first, because extension methods

33
00:02:27,362 --> 00:02:29,390
can't take dynamic arguments.

34
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:35,633
Display Async extends the interface behind the view's Orchard property, not I Orchard

35
00:02:35,633 --> 00:02:39,255
Helper itself, so an injected helper doesn't offer it.

36
00:02:39,255 --> 00:02:43,964
Its display type defaults to an empty string, which means Detail, and it

37
00:02:43,964 --> 00:02:46,680
takes an optional group id and updater.

38
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:55,771
Culture Name and Culture Dir return the name and direction of the current culture.

39
00:02:55,771 --> 00:02:58,050
Is Right To Left returns a Boolean.

40
00:02:58,050 --> 00:03:01,997
A layout uses them to set the language and direction of the page,

41
00:03:01,997 --> 00:03:03,720
and to pick a stylesheet.

42
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:09,827
Asset Url turns a media library path into its public URL, with optional

43
00:03:09,827 --> 00:03:12,332
width, height and resize mode.

44
00:03:12,332 --> 00:03:15,184
Is Image File checks the extension.

45
00:03:15,184 --> 00:03:19,985
Resource Url adds the CDN base URL to a resource path, when one

46
00:03:19,985 --> 00:03:22,420
is set and debug mode is off.

47
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:25,567
Four helpers work on text.

48
00:03:25,567 --> 00:03:31,484
Liquid To HTML Async, Markdown To HTML Async and Shortcodes To HTML Async

49
00:03:31,484 --> 00:03:36,203
render a string as markup, and Sanitize Html cleans HTML.

50
00:03:36,203 --> 00:03:42,270
Markdown To HTML Async sanitizes its result unless you pass sanitize false.

51
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:49,190
For data, Content Query Async runs a saved query by name and returns its content items.

52
00:03:49,190 --> 00:03:54,100
Query List Items Async returns the items of a list, and Get Taxonomy

53
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:58,280
Term Async finds a term from its taxonomy and its own id.

54
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:07,789
A tag helper is an HTML-like element that runs on the server while the view renders.

55
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:11,742
A theme turns each set on with an add Tag Helper directive in

56
00:04:11,742 --> 00:04:16,520
its view imports file, and references the project or package that holds it.

57
00:04:17,270 --> 00:04:20,234
The shape element renders a shape by its type.

58
00:04:20,234 --> 00:04:24,339
The menu element renders a menu by its alias, and the content item

59
00:04:24,339 --> 00:04:27,246
element renders a content item by its handle.

60
00:04:27,246 --> 00:04:32,320
Other attributes become shape properties, and the prop prefix keeps a value's type.

61
00:04:33,070 --> 00:04:36,951
The zone element adds its content to a named zone of the layout,

62
00:04:36,951 --> 00:04:39,279
and renders nothing where it stands.

63
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:43,049
Here a view adds a heading to the Title zone, which the layout

64
00:04:43,049 --> 00:04:46,320
of the admin theme renders with Render Section Async.

65
00:04:47,070 --> 00:04:51,770
A script or style with an asp-name attribute registers a named resource.

66
00:04:51,770 --> 00:04:56,108
A script's at attribute picks Head or Foot; a style renders in the

67
00:04:56,108 --> 00:04:57,976
head unless at is Inline.

68
00:04:57,976 --> 00:05:00,446
The resources element renders them:

69
00:05:00,446 --> 00:05:03,820
Header in the head, Foot Script at the body's end.

70
00:05:04,570 --> 00:05:08,697
The Media module adds attributes to the image element:

71
00:05:08,697 --> 00:05:16,676
asset-src resolves a media library path, and img-width, img-height and img-resize-mode request a resized copy.

72
00:05:16,676 --> 00:05:20,940
Separate videos cover resources and media in more depth.

73
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:26,462
Those are the Orchard helper and the tag helpers of a theme, and

74
00:05:26,462 --> 00:05:29,532
the documentation pages of their modules list the rest.

75
00:05:29,532 --> 00:05:30,840
Thanks for watching.

